## Findings
1. blocking — brief:9 The epoch is read only from `base_sha`, so the switch PR itself has no epoch and receives no ladder checks. If that PR accidentally adds a verdict/red log or ticket entry alongside the setting, the evidence passes unchecked. — check: scripts/ci-certify.test.mjs
2. blocking — brief:10 A candidate-added ticketless log with a valid `# at:` before the epoch is excluded even though the diff proves it is newly introduced; clock skew or an in-flight uncommitted log therefore bypasses certification. The boundary must not trust the artifact’s self-reported time as the condition for checking it. — check: scripts/ci-certify.test.mjs
3. blocking — brief:11 A ticketed `done` PR does add a covered record: Behaviour 5 and the ticket-record promise append a `done` entry to `tickets:`, while line 10 covers every added entry. It therefore does not unconditionally “pass as today” and can fail before the non-opus early return. — check: scripts/ci-certify.test.mjs

